  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Scannable
  displayName: Nikola Bulb
  scientificName: Alga Nox Lux
  description: 'The Nikola Bulb presents a most arresting geometry: five hexagonal
    pads arranged in a flattened constellation upon the rock face, each pulsing with
    violet-white light in what can only be described as a self-congratulatory manner.
    There is something almost electrical about the specimen, and one is advised not
    to place one''s nose too close, as a matter of general prudence.'
  journalImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ea0c194bcc5bf7741ab8b2bc39149241, type: 3}
